.Dd September 30, 2026
.Dt SYSTEM.CONF 5
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm system.conf
.Nd Novi's declared system state
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Pa /etc/novi/system.conf
is the declared state of the machine: not a cache of the
configuration and not a hint to it, but the single document
.Xr novi-state 1
converges the running system to.
.Pp
The format is one
.Ar key No = Ar value
per line.
Blank lines and lines beginning with
.Sq #
are ignored.
Most of the shipped file is commented-out examples, so read a diff of
it for what it
.Em uncomments
as much as for what it adds.
.Pp
The file is meant to be edited by hand.
Settings and
.Nm novi-state set
rewrite one value in place and leave comments and ordering alone, so
an editor and the GUI produce the same document.
.Pp
Declaring a value does not apply it:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
# novi-state diff     where the machine has drifted from this file
# novi-state apply    make the machine match it
# novi-state rollback undo the last apply
.Ed
.Pp
The document is
.Sy additive .
A thing nobody mentions is a thing nothing touches: an account not
named here is not removed, and a package not named here is left as it
is.
The anchor key is what brings something under management.
.Sh KEYS
.Ss Identity
.Bl -tag -width "network.firewall.allow" -compact
.It Va hostname
The system hostname.
.El
.Ss This engine's own behaviour
.Bl -tag -width "network.firewall.allow" -compact
.It Va state.apply_on_boot
.Cm on | off .
Converge at every boot, not only when asked.
.El
.Ss Services
.Bl -tag -width "network.firewall.allow" -compact
.It Va services.\& Ns Ar name
.Cm on | off .
An
s6-rc(8)
service.
.El
.Ss Network
.Bl -tag -width "network.firewall.allow" -compact
.It Va network.dhcp
.Cm on | off .
The DHCP client
.Em service .
A machine may have this on and run no DHCP client: the key predates
static addressing and names the service rather than the protocol.
.It Va network.interface
.Cm auto | Ar name .
Which interface to use.
.It Va network.address
.Cm dhcp | Ar addr Ns / Ns Ar prefix .
A bare address without a prefix is refused rather than assumed to be
/24: the prefix decides which hosts this machine believes are local,
and guessing produces a machine that reaches some destinations and not
others.
.It Va network.gateway
.Cm auto | Cm none | Ar addr .
.It Va network.address6
.Cm auto | Cm none | Ar addr Ns / Ns Ar prefix .
.Cm auto
is SLAAC.
There is deliberately no
.Cm dhcp :
DHCPv6 is a different protocol that the shipped client does not speak,
and a word that reads as supported and does nothing is worse than its
absence.
.It Va network.gateway6
.Cm auto | Cm none | Ar addr .
.It Va network.dns
.Cm auto | Ar addr Ns Oo , Ns Ar addr Oc Ns ... .
A declared list beats the lease.
With a static address and
.Cm auto
there is no lease, so there is no resolver; the service says so on
startup.
.It Va network.wifi
.Cm on | off .
The supplicant.
Credentials are not declared here \(em see
.Xr novi-wifi 1 .
.It Va network.wifi.interface
.Cm auto | Ar name .
.It Va network.firewall
.Cm on | off .
Loads
.Pa /etc/novi/firewall.nft .
.It Va network.firewall.allow
.Cm none | Ar port Ns Oo , Ns Ar port Ns Oo / Ns Ar proto Oc Oc Ns ... .
Ports let in.
This is a
.Sy separate key
from
.Va services.\& Ns Ar name
on purpose: a firewall that opens itself because a daemon started is a
service registry with a policy file attached.
The set of things reachable from the network has to be one list a
person chose.
Ports are numbers, never names.
.El
.Ss Users
.Bl -tag -width "network.firewall.allow" -compact
.It Va users.\& Ns Ar name Ns Va .shell
A path, or
.Cm absent .
This is the anchor key: declaring it creates the account, and
.Cm absent
removes it.
Removing an account never deletes the home directory.
.It Va users.\& Ns Ar name Ns Va .groups
A comma-separated list, or
.Cm none .
.El
.Ss Packages
.Bl -tag -width "network.firewall.allow" -compact
.It Va packages.\& Ns Ar name
.Cm present | absent .
A removal another installed package still depends on is
.Sy refused ,
which is permanent drift and the honest report: the machine does not
match the document and this engine will not make it.
.El
.Ss Display
.Bl -tag -width "network.firewall.allow" -compact
.It Va display.renderer
.Cm pixman | gles2 | auto .
Measured under identical load in QEMU, pixman used 363 CPU ticks
against gles2's 1998, because software rasterisation through a GL API
is more work than drawing 2D directly.
On hardware with a real driver the answer inverts, which is why this
is a key.
.It Va display.theme
A file in
.Pa /usr/share/novi/themes ,
shadowed by one of the same name in
.Pa /etc/novi/themes .
Colour only.
.El
.Ss Power
.Bl -tag -width "network.firewall.allow" -compact
.It Va power.blank
.Ar seconds | Cm off .
Idle screen blank.
.It Va power.suspend
.Ar seconds | Cm off .
Idle suspend.
Off by default: blanking a screen is undone by moving the mouse,
suspending only by a working wake path.
.It Va power.suspend.lock
.Cm on | off .
Lock before an idle suspend.
On by default, and the machine does not suspend if the lock screen
fails to appear.
.It Va power.lid.lock
.Cm on | off .
Lock before a lid-close suspend.
This one sleeps either way after waiting: a closed lid is a machine in
a bag.
.It Va power.lid
.It Va power.button
.Cm suspend | poweroff | ignore .
.It Va power.governor
A CPU frequency governor.
.Nm novi-power governors
lists the ones this kernel has.
Not set by default.
.El
.Ss Storage
.Bl -tag -width "network.firewall.allow" -compact
.It Va storage.automount
.Cm on | off .
Removable media appear under
.Pa /run/media .
.El
.Ss Agent
.Bl -tag -width "network.firewall.allow" -compact
.It Va agent.enabled
.Cm on | off .
Whether
.Xr novi-agent 1
may
.Em change
anything.
Reading is always allowed.
.It Va agent.allow
.Cm none | Ar verb Ns Oo , Ns Ar verb Oc Ns ... .
Two keys rather than one, for the same reason as the firewall.
.It Va agent.rate
.Ar calls-per-minute | Cm off .
This bounds an accident and is not a security control: anything that
can run
.Xr novi-agent 1
can run
.Xr pkg 1
directly.
.El
.Sh KEYS THAT CANNOT DRIFT
.Va power.blank ,
.Va power.lid ,
.Va power.button ,
.Va storage.automount
and the
.Va agent.*
keys are read when they are used rather than held by anything.
Nothing converges them, so
.Nm novi-state apply
has nothing to do for them and an unusable value is reported by
.Nm novi-state diff
as
.Sy unsupported .
That report is where a typo in one of them surfaces.
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width "/var/lib/novi-state" -compact
.It Pa /etc/novi/system.conf
This file.
.It Pa /etc/shadow
Password hashes.
Deliberately not declared here: this file is world-readable and is
meant to be committed to version control.
Configuration is declared; secrets are not.
.It Pa /etc/novi/wifi.conf
WiFi passphrases, for the same reason.
.El
.Sh EXAMPLES
A machine with a static address, a firewall hole for ssh, and no idle
suspend:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
hostname               = workshop
network.address        = 192.168.1.50/24
network.gateway        = 192.168.1.1
network.dns            = 1.1.1.1,9.9.9.9
network.firewall       = on
network.firewall.allow = 22
services.sshd          = on
power.suspend          = off
.Ed
.Sh DIAGNOSTICS
A key this build does not recognise is reported as
.Sy unmanaged
rather than refused, so a document written for a newer Novi still
applies on an older one.
A misspelled key therefore reads as declarative, looks converged to
anyone skimming, and converges nothing.
.Nm novi-state diff
is where it shows up.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr novi-agent 1 ,
.Xr novi-power 1 ,
.Xr novi-state 1 ,
.Xr novi-wifi 1 ,
.Xr pkg 1
.Sh STANDARDS
RFC 0002,
.Pa /usr/share/doc/novi/rfcs/0002-declarative-system-state.md .
.Sh CAVEATS
Adding a
.Va network.firewall.allow
port does not start a service, and enabling a service does not open a
port.
Both keys are exactly as declared, so
.Nm novi-state diff
cannot report the mismatch;
.Nm novi-state
prints a note about it instead.
